[gd_scene load_steps=2 format=3]

; The same plume as unit-cpuparticles2d.tscn with `use_fixed_seed` and `seed` REMOVED.
; That absence is the ONE variable: same amount, same lifetime, same preprocess, same
; fixed_fps, same emission shape and velocities, so every pixel that moves relative to
; that fixture is the seed and nothing else.
;
; Godot randomises `seed` in its constructor when use_fixed_seed is off and never
; serialises it, so THE ENGINE cannot draw this scene the same way twice. The previewer
; can, and must: it substitutes a fixed seed, which is what lets a scene the author
; never pinned still open identically every time. Every other emitter fixture in the bag
; pins seed and preprocess — that is what makes their poses comparable against Godot,
; and it is also why the substitution itself is exercised by nothing else. Drop it and
; every gate stays green while the previewer starts drawing a different flame per open.
;
; THIS BASELINE IS NOT A GODOT-PARITY CLAIM. It records our substituted pose. There is
; no reference render to arbitrate it against, because a second reference render would
; not match the first.

